  "infoGuidelinesTitle": "Community guidelines",
  "infoGuidelinesBody": "# Be real\nShare your own work and say when content is AI-generated or taken from a source.\n\n# Be kind\nNo harassment, hate or threats. Disagree without attacking people.\n\n# Keep it safe\nNo sexual exploitation, graphic violence, self-harm promotion, scams or illegal goods. Content involving minors is removed immediately.\n\n# Earn reach fairly\nFake engagement, bots and view manipulation are not allowed. Reach Levels count qualified viewers only.\n\n# Appeals\nIf we remove something you can appeal and a person will review it.",
  "infoPrivacyTitle": "Privacy policy",
  "infoPrivacyBody": "# What we collect\nOnly what BLOCKS needs: your profile, your posts and your district — never your exact GPS location.\n\n# What we never do\nWe do not sell your personal data. Advertisers reach interest groups, not individuals.\n\n# Your controls\nUse Safety Center and Settings to control privacy, messages and notifications. You can request your data or delete your account.\n\n# Payments and identity\nPayout and identity details are stored separately from your public profile.\n\n# Demo note\nThis is summary copy for the prototype, not a legal policy.",
  "infoTermsTitle": "Terms of service",
  "infoTermsBody": "# Using BLOCKS\nYou must be old enough to use social media in your country and follow the Community Guidelines.\n\n# Your content\nYou own what you post and let BLOCKS show it to other people.\n\n# Creator rewards\nRewards come from a pool shared by qualified reach. They are estimates until finalised and are never a promise of a rupee amount per view.\n\n# Demo note\nThis is summary copy for the prototype, not legal terms.",
  "infoHelpTitle": "Help & support",
  "infoHelpBody": "# How do Reach Levels work?\nPosts climb District, State, National and Global as real people in more places engage with them.\n\n# Why is my post still at District level?\nOnly qualified views count. Open the Rising tab to see how close it is.\n\n# How do I get verified?\nOpen Profile, then Menu, then Verification and request a badge.\n\n# How do I report something?\nTap the three dots on a post, reel or profile and choose Report.\n\n# Need a person?\nThis is a demo, so there is no live support.",
